# CODEOWNERS for the Golden Path kit repository (krnese/golden-path).
#
# What it does: GitHub requests a review from the listed owner on every pull request that touches a matching
# path. The LAST matching pattern wins, so the explicit lines below override the default '*' line; keep them
# owned by the same person unless you mean to change who reviews that path.
#
# Enforcement is OFF on purpose. The ruleset 'Golden Path main' has "Require review from Code Owners"
# disabled because this repository has a single maintainer, and GitHub does not let a PR author approve
# their own PR. Turning the rule on now would lock the maintainer out of merging. This file routes review
# requests and documents ownership; it does not block merges today.
#
# To enable enforcement safely later:
#   1. Add a second owner (for example a colleague, as an individual @user) to the lines below and merge
#      that change first, so every owned path has someone other than the author who can approve.
#   2. Then, in Settings > Rules > 'Golden Path main', turn on "Require review from Code Owners".
# Alternative for a sole maintainer: add the repository admin role as a bypass actor with mode
# "pull request only" (bypass allowed only through a PR, never by direct push), document that choice in
# docs/LEVEL-2.md, and only then enable the rule.
#
# Copilot code review reads instructions from the PR head branch, so instruction files are owner-reviewed.

*                                   @krnese

# Kit source and installer
/plugin/                            @krnese

# Installed kit, automation and agent instructions
/.github/                           @krnese
/.github/hooks/                     @krnese
/.github/skills/                    @krnese
/.github/prompts/                   @krnese
/.github/workflows/                 @krnese
/.github/scripts/                   @krnese
/.github/copilot-instructions.md    @krnese
/.github/instructions/              @krnese
/AGENTS.md                          @krnese
/.golden-path/config.json           @krnese

# Kit tests and the demo's business acceptance and tasks
/tests/                             @krnese
/examples/invoice-demo/acceptance/  @krnese
/examples/invoice-demo/tasks/       @krnese

# This file itself (last, so nothing above can override it)
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @krnese
